```php
namespace AzGuard\Contracts\Scopes;

#[Spi(kind: SpiKind::Implement, since: '1.0')]
interface DescribesAssignmentScope extends AssignmentScopeDefinition
{
    /** Facts core needs about this definition; pure, no I/O, same answer for the lifetime of the object. */
    public function description(): AssignmentScopeDescription;
}
```
```php
namespace AzGuard\Context;

#[Spi(kind: SpiKind::Call, since: '1.0')]
final readonly class AssignmentScopeDescription
{
    /**
     * @param list<object|class-string> $components configuration only the panel's evaluator applies (for the Scopes
     *        module: its filters), in declaration order; opaque to core
     * @param class-string<AssignmentScopeDirectory>|null $directory default directory of the alias
     * @param bool $tenantOwner false: every record belongs to the global tenant (no owner callback)
     * @param bool $resolvesThroughQuery true: resolve() equals query() + tenantOf() for every ref
     */
    public function __construct(
        public array $components = [],
        public ?string $label = null,
        public ?string $directory = null,
        public bool $tenantOwner = true,
        public bool $resolvesThroughQuery = false,
    ) {}
}
```
A definition that does not implement `DescribesAssignmentScope` is treated as `new AssignmentScopeDescription()` (core-internal helper, e.g. a static `describe(AssignmentScopeDefinition)` in `Context\Internal\ContextIdentity` or the compiler — an existing class, rule 5).

Module side: `Scopes\BaseAssignmentScope implements DescribesAssignmentScope` (in addition to its current interfaces): `components` = `settings()->filters`, `label`/`directory` from `settings()`, `tenantOwner` = `true` except `ModelAssignmentScopeDefinition` → `hasOwner()`, `resolvesThroughQuery` = `resolve()` is declared by `BaseAssignmentScope` (today's reflection check of `ScopeConfiguration::resolvesByQuery`).

| Core site today | Target |
|:--|:--|
| `PanelCompiler::compile` → `ScopeConfiguration::checkOptions` | removed from core; `ScopesPlugin::register()` throws `DefinitionException` for an adapter alias outside its own definitions (same message text: `… registers an access adapter for unknown assignment scope …`) and for a membership/adapter that is not an object or class-string of its contract; container resolvability → `scopes.membership` doctor finding (error) |
| `PanelCompiler::scopes` → `tenantOwner` | `TenantMode::Required && ! description->tenantOwner` → `InvalidConfigurationException::failing('tenant_scope', …)` (same text) |
| `PanelCompiler::scopes` / `RoleCompiler` → `filterMetadata !== []` without evaluator | `description->components !== []` |
| `PanelCompiler::scopes` → `sameStructure` + `merge` | same class, `type()`, `model()` and `CanonicalMetadata::componentMetadata($existing) == …($definition)` → keep the first; else `DefinitionException` "declares conflicting assignment scope definitions for <alias>"; no merge |
| `PanelCompiler::scopeDirectories` → `ScopeConfiguration::directory` | `description->directory` |
| `PanelFingerprint` → `filterMetadata`, `membership`, `adapters` | `'configuration' => CanonicalMetadata::componentMetadata($definition)` plus `array_map(componentMetadata, description->components)`; `membership`/`adapters` entries removed (module options are already fingerprinted under `options`; a test proves a changed membership or adapter changes the fingerprint) |
| `RoleCompiler` `filter_configuration` | `array_map(fn ($c) => hash('sha256', json_encode(CanonicalMetadata::componentMetadata($c), JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR)), description->components)` |
| `ResourceContextMapping` → `ownerless`, `resolvesByQuery` | `! description->tenantOwner`, `description->resolvesThroughQuery` |
| `BatchInputs` → reflection against `BaseAssignmentScope` | `description->resolvesThroughQuery` (with `QueryableAssignmentScopeDefinition`) |
| `SchemaBuilder` → `RoleBindings::of`, `ConfigurableAssignmentScopeDefinition::settings()`, `ScopeConfiguration::adapters` | core enumerates `BaseRole::scopes()` itself (container-resolve class strings; same alias; same class and model as the registered definition else `DefinitionException`); filters = class names of `description->components` (`Closure` for a closure), label = binding label ?? registered label ?? `scopeLabel()`, directory = binding `description->directory`, `exactSupport` = `#amendments` |

After P3.1 no file under `packages/core/src` outside `src/Scopes`, `src/Audit`, `src/Plugins/Audit` references `AzGuard\Scopes\*` or `Contracts\Scopes\ConfigurableAssignmentScopeDefinition` (i2.json entries of `BatchInputs.php` and `SchemaBuilder.php` removed).
